- bufio - Buffered I/O

+ golang
+ stdlib
+ docs-analysis
+ bufio

 "Discover Packages Standard library bufio"
      " (contain) "import path"
           " (contain) "Discover Packages Standard library bufio"
      " (contain) documentation
           " (contain) "Package bufio implements buffered I/O. It wraps an io.Reader or io.Writer object, creating another object (Reader or Writer) that also implements the interface but provides buffering and some help for textual I/O."
      " (contain) functions
           " (contain) ScanBytes
                " (contain) signature
                     " (contain) "func ScanBytes(data []byte, atEOF bool) (advance int, token []byte, err error)"
                " (contain) description
                     " (contain) "ScanBytes is a split function for a Scanner that returns each byte as a token."
           " (contain) ScanLines
                " (contain) signature
                     " (contain) "func ScanLines(data []byte, atEOF bool) (advance int, token []byte, err error)"
                " (contain) description
                     " (contain) "ScanLines is a split function for a Scanner that returns each line of text, stripped of any trailing end-of-line marker. The returned line may be empty. The end-of-line marker is one optional carriage return followed by one mandatory newline. In regular expression notation, it is `\r?\n`. The last non-empty line of input will be returned even if it has no newline."
           " (contain) ScanRunes
                " (contain) signature
                     " (contain) "func ScanRunes(data []byte, atEOF bool) (advance int, token []byte, err error)"
                " (contain) description
                     " (contain) "ScanRunes is a split function for a Scanner that returns each UTF-8-encoded rune as a token. The sequence of runes returned is equivalent to that from a range loop over the input as a string, which means that erroneous UTF-8 encodings translate to U+FFFD = '\xef\xbf\xbd'. Because of the Scan interface, this makes it impossible for the client to distinguish correctly encoded replacement runes from encoding errors."
           " (contain) ScanWords
                " (contain) signature
                     " (contain) "func ScanWords(data []byte, atEOF bool) (advance int, token []byte, err error)"
                " (contain) description
                     " (contain) "ScanWords is a split function for a Scanner that returns each space-separated word of text, with surrounding spaces deleted. It will never return an empty string. The definition of space is set by unicode.IsSpace."
      " (contain) types
           " (contain) ReadWriter
                " (contain) kind
                     " (contain) struct
                " (contain) description
                     " (contain) "ReadWriter stores pointers to a Reader and a Writer. It implements io.ReadWriter."
           " (contain) Reader
                " (contain) kind
                     " (contain) struct
                " (contain) description
                     " (contain) "Reader implements buffering for an io.Reader object. A new Reader is created by calling NewReader or NewReaderSize; alternatively the zero value of a Reader may be used after calling [Reset] on it."
           " (contain) Scanner
                " (contain) kind
                     " (contain) struct
                " (contain) description
                     " (contain) "Scanner provides a convenient interface for reading data such as a file of newline-delimited lines of text. Successive calls to the Scanner.Scan method will step through the 'tokens' of a file, skipping the bytes between the tokens. The specification of a token is defined by a split function of type SplitFunc; the default split function breaks the input into lines with line termination stripped. Scanner.Split functions are defined in this package for scanning a file into lines, bytes, UTF-8-enco..."
           " (contain) SplitFunc
                " (contain) kind
                     " (contain) other
                " (contain) description
                     " (contain) "SplitFunc is the signature of the split function used to tokenize the input. The arguments are an initial substring of the remaining unprocessed data and a flag, atEOF, that reports whether the Reader has no more data to give. The return values are the number of bytes to advance the input and the next token to return to the user, if any, plus an error, if any."
           " (contain) Writer
                " (contain) kind
                     " (contain) struct
                " (contain) description
                     " (contain) "Writer implements buffering for an io.Writer object. If an error occurs writing to a Writer, no more data will be accepted and all subsequent writes, and Writer.Flush, will return the error. After all data has been written, the client should call the Writer.Flush method to guarantee all data has been forwarded to the underlying io.Writer."
